{"scope":"rt-647c54a19c","css":".rt-647c54a19c p.MsoNormal, .rt-647c54a19c li.MsoNormal, .rt-647c54a19c div.MsoNormal {margin:0cm; font-size:10.0pt; font-family:\"Times New Roman\",serif;}\n.rt-647c54a19c p.MsoListParagraph, .rt-647c54a19c li.MsoListParagraph, .rt-647c54a19c div.MsoListParagraph {margin-top:0cm; margin-right:0cm; margin-bottom:0cm; margin-left:36.0pt; font-size:10.0pt; font-family:\"Times New Roman\",serif;}\n.rt-647c54a19c div.WordSection1 {}\n.rt-647c54a19c ol {margin-bottom:0cm;}\n.rt-647c54a19c ul {margin-bottom:0cm;}","html":"<div class=WordSection1>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=EN-US>.<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span style='position:relative;z-index:251657728;left:-52px;\r\ntop:22px;width:994px;height:24px'><img width=795 height=2\r\nsrc=\"data:image\/gif;base64,R0lGODlh4gMCAHcAMSH+GlNvZnR3YXJlOiBNaWNyb3NvZnQgT2ZmaWNlACH5BAEAAAAALAAAAADiAwIAgAAAAAAAAAJUhI+py+0Po5y02ouz3rz7D4biSJbmiabqyrbuCycBMNf0bef4rvf87wsCh8Ii8WhMIpfKJvPpjEKn0ir1as1it9ou9+sNg8fiMvlsTqPX6jb7DSgAADs=\"><\/span><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:14.0pt;\r\nfont-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<br clear=ALL>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:14.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>DEPARTMENT OF\r\nRADIOLOGY &amp; IMAGING<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\r\n<\/span><b><u><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>USG\r\nOF LEFT\/RIGHT \u00a0SHOULDER<\/span><\/u><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:16.0pt'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\r\n<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Study\r\nof shoulder shows normal architecture of both supraspinatous muscle and tendon.No\u00a0\r\nobvious partial &amp; full thickness tear noted in subdeltoid bursa under\r\nleft\/right deltoid muscle.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Deltoid\r\nmuscle appears normal in echogenecity and\u00a0 texture.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Right\/left\r\n\u00a0infraspinatous muscle appears normal in echotexture with normal beck-like\r\ninsertion.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Right\/left\r\nsubscapularis muscle shows normal echotexture with normally oriented fibres.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Right\r\n\/left teres minor muscle appears normal in echotexture(as far as visualised) <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Right\r\n\/left biceps brachii tendon in biccipital grove appears normal in thickness and\r\nechotexture.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Synovial\r\nsheath around biceps tendon in Biccipital groove shows minimal fluid collection\r\n.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Humeral\r\nhead appears smooth in appearance with normal hypoechoice articular cartilage\r\nsurrounding it.No significant effusion noted around humeral head.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Greater\r\ntuberosity of left\/right humerus appears normal with no obvious significant\r\nsurface <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><u><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>IMRESSION\u00a0 :<\/span><\/u><\/b><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'> \u00a0\u00a0NORMAL STUDY<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:14.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>DEPARTMENT OF\r\nRADIOLOGY &amp; IMAGING<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\r\n<\/span><b><u><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>USG\r\nOF RIGHT SHOULDER JOINT<\/span><\/u><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:16.0pt'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<ul style='margin-top:0cm' type=disc>\r\n <li class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>The\r\n     long head of biceps tendon appears intact with<b> mild collection of fluid\r\n     around the biceps tendon.<\/b><\/span><\/li>\r\n<\/ul>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<ul style='margin-top:0cm' type=disc>\r\n <li class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Subscapularis\r\n     tendon and infraspinatous tendon appear intact.<\/span><\/li>\r\n<\/ul>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<ul style='margin-top:0cm' type=disc>\r\n <li class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n     \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Heterogenecity with ? partial thickness tear is\r\n     seen in the supraspinatus tendon before insertion point over the gleno-humeral\r\n     joint. There is <\/span><\/b><\/li>\r\n<\/ul>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>hypoechoic\r\ncollection around the insertion point.<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<ul style='margin-top:0cm' type=disc>\r\n <li class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n     \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Multiple focal abnormality is seen within\r\n     supraspinatus tendon at the<\/span><\/b><\/li>\r\n<\/ul>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u00a0insertion\r\npoint. <\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoListParagraph><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<ul style='margin-top:0cm' type=disc>\r\n <li class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n     \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>A minimal amount of peritendinous collection is\r\n     seen around <\/span><\/b><\/li>\r\n<\/ul>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>the\r\nsupraspinatus and subscapularis tendon.<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<ul style='margin-top:0cm' type=disc>\r\n <li class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Subdeltoid\r\n     bursa appears normal without any evidence bursal effusion.<\/span><\/li>\r\n<\/ul>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<ul style='margin-top:0cm' type=disc>\r\n <li class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>No\r\n     bony irregularities and\/or cortical irregularities seen in humeral head. <\/span><\/li>\r\n<\/ul>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\r\n<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><u><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>IMRESSION\u00a0 :<\/span><\/u><\/b><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<ol style='margin-top:0cm' start=1 type=1>\r\n <li class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n     \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>HETEROGENECITY WITH ? PARTIAL THICKNESS TEAR IN\r\n     THE <\/span><\/b><\/li>\r\n<\/ol>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>SUPRASPINATUS\r\nTENDON.<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<ol style='margin-top:0cm' start=2 type=1>\r\n <li class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n     \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>FOCAL HYPERECHOGENICITY IS SEEN NEAR THE\r\n     INSERTION POINT OF SUPRASPINATUS AS DESCRIBED.<\/span><\/b><\/li>\r\n <li class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n     \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>MILD PERITENDINOUS COLLECTION AROUND THE\r\n     SUPRASPINATUS AND SUBSCAPULARIS TENDON.<\/span><\/b><\/li>\r\n<\/ol>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Suggested : Clinical correlation &amp; other\r\nrelevant investigations.<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<\/div>","page":{"size":"612.0pt 792.0pt","margin":"151.2pt 36.0pt 72.0pt 36.0pt"}}